OL,3,GNEWSALocal patient watchdogs to stay
OL,4,Aopen after U-turn
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than 150 patient watchdogs
OL,7,Fincluding six in Bedfordshire,
OL,8,FHertfordshire and Buckinghamshire will
OL,9,Fstay open following a government
OL,10,FU-turn.
OL,12,FLast year it was announced Healthwatch
OL,13,Fboards, which advocate on behalf of
OL,14,Fpatients, would be abolished as part of
OL,15,Fa 10-year health plan to reduce
OL,16,Fbureaucracy.
OL,18,FHealth Secretary Yvette Cooper said:
OL,19,F"We will retain Healthwatch England and
OL,20,FLocal Healthwatch, while strengthening
OL,21,Fthem to ensure patient voices are heard
OL,22,Fand can influence real change."
OL,23,APub: 04-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,373,370,200,160,0,100
